# D-DISKROMHOST step 2 (2026-11-24): zerobas's disk ROM as a cartridge in the VG-8020, and the references' H.RUNC.
# scratchpad/diskhost_probe.py MACHINE EXT DISK SECONDS [KEYS]; DISK = a private copy of an MSX-DOS 1.03 + COMMAND 1.11 disk.
# SYM lines: zerobas's OWN disk-ROM labels (build/disk.sym), traced only while page 1 is a non-slot-0 slot holding our ROM.
# H.RUNC-all-RET: $FECB..$FECF all $C9 (RAM).

## BEFORE (e807c097d's disk ROM): the DOS boot runs from INIT, in the boot scan
### Philips_VG_8020 + zerobas-disk, disk msxdos103-cmd111.dsk, 20.0 s, keys ''
HRUNC 1.1909 SP=F09A HIMEM=F380
=== SCREEN 3 s HIMEM=F380 H.RUNC-is-RET=1
  |           MSX  system          
  |           version 1.0          
  |   Copyright 1983 by Microsoft  
SYM init 4.9521 SP=F08E HIMEM=F380
SYM boot_disk_go 4.9550 SP=F08E HIMEM=DE77
SYM dos_handoff 5.1819 SP=F08C HIMEM=DE77
HIT0100 6.590 SCRMOD=1 LINLEN=29 HIMEM=DE77
=== SCREEN 8 s HIMEM=DE77 H.RUNC-is-RET=1
  |  MSX-DOS version 1.03          
  |  Copyright 1984 by Microsoft   
HIT0100 11.650 SCRMOD=1 LINLEN=29 HIMEM=DE77
=== SCREEN 19 s HIMEM=DE77 H.RUNC-is-RET=1
  |  MSX-DOS version 1.03          
  |  Copyright 1984 by Microsoft   
  |  COMMAND version 1.11          
  |  Current date is Sun 84-01-01  
  |  Enter new date:               
hits0100 2

# (H.RUNC-is-RET above = the old name of H.RUNC-all-RET; no SYM hrunc_h/init_p2: those labels did not exist)

## AFTER: INIT is phase 1; the cold start's H.RUNC runs phase 2 and boots MSX-DOS
### Philips_VG_8020 + zerobas-disk, disk msxdos103-cmd111.dsk, 20.0 s, keys ''
HRUNC 1.1909 SP=F09A HIMEM=F380
=== SCREEN 3 s HIMEM=F380 H.RUNC-all-RET=1 H.RUNC-byte0=c9
  |           MSX  system          
  |           version 1.0          
  |   Copyright 1983 by Microsoft  
SYM init 4.9521 SP=F08E HIMEM=F380
HRUNC 4.9581 SP=F09A HIMEM=DE77
SYM hrunc_h 4.9583 SP=F094 HIMEM=DE77
SYM init_p2 4.9583 SP=F094 HIMEM=DE77
SYM boot_disk_go 4.9591 SP=F094 HIMEM=DE77
SYM dos_handoff 4.9863 SP=F092 HIMEM=DE77
HIT0100 6.394 SCRMOD=1 LINLEN=29 HIMEM=DE77
=== SCREEN 8 s HIMEM=DE77 H.RUNC-all-RET=1 H.RUNC-byte0=c9
  |  MSX-DOS version 1.03          
  |  Copyright 1984 by Microsoft   
HIT0100 11.658 SCRMOD=1 LINLEN=29 HIMEM=DE77
=== SCREEN 19 s HIMEM=DE77 H.RUNC-all-RET=1 H.RUNC-byte0=c9
  |  MSX-DOS version 1.03          
  |  Copyright 1984 by Microsoft   
  |  COMMAND version 1.11          
  |  Current date is Sun 84-01-01  
  |  Enter new date:               
hits0100 2


## AFTER, no disk: BASIC comes up; the layout is still HIMEM $F380's (unchanged from before, see BEFORE below)
### Philips_VG_8020 + zerobas-disk, disk none, 30.0 s, keys '12:PRINT FRE(0);FRE("");HEX$(PEEK(&HFC4A)+256*PEEK(&HFC4B))\\r'
HRUNC 1.1909 SP=F09A HIMEM=F380
SYM init 4.9521 SP=F08E HIMEM=F380
HRUNC 4.9581 SP=F09A HIMEM=DE77
SYM hrunc_h 4.9583 SP=F094 HIMEM=DE77
SYM init_p2 4.9583 SP=F094 HIMEM=DE77
SYM boot_disk_go 4.9591 SP=F094 HIMEM=DE77
=== SCREEN 11 s HIMEM=DE77 H.RUNC-all-RET=1 H.RUNC-byte0=c9
  |  MSX BASIC version 1.0                 
  |  Copyright 1983 by Microsoft           
  |  28815 Bytes free                      
  |  Ok                                    
  |  color  auto   goto   list   run       
=== SCREEN 29 s HIMEM=DE77 H.RUNC-all-RET=1 H.RUNC-byte0=c9
  |  MSX BASIC version 1.0                 
  |  Copyright 1983 by Microsoft           
  |  28815 Bytes free                      
  |  Ok                                    
  |  PRINT FRE(0);FRE("");HEX$(PEEK(&HFC4A 
  |  )+256*PEEK(&HFC4B))                   
  |   28815  200 DE77                      
  |  Ok                                    
  |  color  auto   goto   list   run       
hits0100 0

